message: "If you use these materials, please cite them as follows."
authors:
  - family-names: "Boushey"
    given-names: "Geoffrey"
    affiliation: "UCSF Library"
title: "Research and Patent Landscape Informatics"
version: 1.0.0
date-released: 2026-11-13
url: "https://github.com/UCSF-DSOS/Research-Patent-Landscape-Workshop"
abstract: >-
  A workshop curriculum for computational research and patent landscape
  informatics. The repository introduces methods for retrieving and
  analyzing scholarly research, grant, and patent information using
  OpenAlex, Dimensions, the USPTO Open Data Portal, Google Patents,
  and Google BigQuery. Applied examples use Python, APIs, JSON, pandas,
  SQL, and network analysis to explore relationships among researchers,
  inventors, research funding, and patents. A capstone workflow combines
  USPTO patent data with locally running generative AI models through
  Ollama for OCR, patent summarization, image analysis, and prior-art
  relevance screening.
